Template: product-rating/purge-data
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Remove the product-rating database, photos and log files?
 The package is being purged. Its data directory /var/lib/product-rating
 holds the SQLite database and every uploaded photo, and
 /var/log/product-rating holds the log files, if file logging was switched
 on.
 .
 Confirm this only if that data is meant to be gone for good; short of a
 backup there is no way back. Declining keeps both directories, so a later
 install of the package finds its products, photos and accounts again.
 .
 The configuration in /etc/product-rating, including the session secret, is
 removed either way - that is what purging a package means.
